The compounded run detects **fewer** quirks than the isolated runs. That is a
result, not a defect: Q2, Q9 and Q11 change which transactions land on which
business day, so the daily balances Q3 and Q6 accrue interest on are no longer
the shadow's, and the exact day-count ratio those two would otherwise show is
destroyed. Reporting only the compounded number would understate what continuous
reconciliation can do; reporting only the isolated number would overstate it.

